course: dictionary
lesson: 10668
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word unlock has more than one meaning. The meaning that fits depends on the words around it. «Ruby unlocked her brother's phone to look at his games.» Here unlock means to open something with a code, so the phone can be used.
explain: «The game's battle pass unlocked a new character.» Nothing is opened with a key here. In a game, to unlock means to make something new available. Ask yourself: what would fit in the sentence? Then test your meaning by putting it in place of the word.
explain: Unlock can also mean to discover or free something hidden. «Practice can unlock a talent you did not know you had.» The talent was inside you all along, and practice helps you find it. Read the whole sentence, not just the word.
fact: Unlock means to open a lock, or to make a device usable, often with a code, pattern or fingerprint.
fact: In games, unlock means to make a new level, character or item available.
fact: Unlock can also mean to discover or free something hidden, like a secret or a talent.
fact: The opposite of unlock is lock, which means to close something so it cannot be opened without a key or code.
fact: Good context clues are the words near the word, such as «phone», «game» or «secret», which show which meaning is right.
exercise: «Ruby unlocked her brother's phone to look at his games.» What does unlocked mean here? | Put it in a bag | Lost it for ever | *Opened it with a code so it could be used | Dropped it on the floor
exercise: «Playing every day unlocked a new level.» What does unlocked mean here? | Turned the game off | Made the game slower | *Made a new level available | Broke the level
exercise: «A boy left his bike unlocked outside a shop.» Find and copy the word that shows the bike was not locked. | outside | shop | bike | *unlocked
test: Dad says, «Please unlock the car.» What does unlock mean? | Paint the car | Count the keys | *Open the lock with a key or button | Close the door tightly
test: «Practice can unlock a talent you did not know you had.» Which meaning fits? | *Discover and free something hidden | Forget a skill you once had | Lose something important | Buy a new game
exam: «Imagine unlocking the other ninety!» Which meaning of unlock fits best? | Lock them away again | Sell them for money | *Make them available or discover them | Count them slowly
